[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328148359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110852#issuecomment-3328148359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110852","id":3328148359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GX4OH","user":{"login":"ernzo","id":5151357,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTEzNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5151357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo","html_url":"https://github.com/ernzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T12:21:02Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T12:21:02Z","body":"Not en expert, but I'd say,\nIf your app does Not use C#/Mono there's a possibility..\n\n-You will need to generate custom Android Templates.\n\nIn the file godot/platform/android/detect.py, you got to add this line on the \"# Link flags\" section :\nenv.Append(LINKFLAGS=[\"-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384\"])\n\n```\n# Link flags\n\n    env.Append(LINKFLAGS=[\"-Wl,--gc-sections\", \"-Wl,--no-undefined\", \"-Wl,-z,now\"])\n    env.Append(LINKFLAGS=[\"-Wl,--build-id\"])\n    env.Append(LINKFLAGS=[\"-Wl,-soname,libgodot_android.so\"])\n    # Add 16KB page alignment for modern Android targets.\n    env.Append(LINKFLAGS=[\"-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384\"])\n```\n\nThis will make Godot's internal libgodot_android.so be aligned to 16KB\n\nAt least that worked with Godot Mono 4.5dev3,\nand seems to work with 4.5 Stable, although it may be redundant in this context.\n\n-What this will Not do is align the Mono libraries to 16kb..\n\nAnd you will still get the dreaded message:\nLibraries that do not support 16 KB:\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libSystem.Globalization.Native.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libSystem.IO.Compression.Native.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libSystem.Native.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libSystem.Security.Cryptography.Native.Android.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libmono-component-debugger.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libmono-component-diagnostics_tracing.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libmono-component-hot_reload.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libmono-component-marshal-ilgen.so\nbase/lib/arm64-v8a/libmonosgen-2.0.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libSystem.Globalization.Native.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libSystem.IO.Compression.Native.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libSystem.Native.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libSystem.Security.Cryptography.Native.Android.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libmono-component-debugger.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libmono-component-diagnostics_tracing.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libmono-component-hot_reload.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libmono-component-marshal-ilgen.so\nbase/lib/x86_64/libmonosgen-2.0.so\n\n-To fix that, a pretty considerable refactoring of Godot Mono 4.5 was necessary (as far as I can tell),\nit took months and a few releases to do it cleanly, so it's not an Easy task..\n\nMaybe more Experienced devs can shed some light, tell us what that restructure really involved..\n\n-What's the purpose tho..\nMore security?\n\nNew Godot versions break your app?\n\n-And what about macOS and Xcode...?\nCould you tell us your experience?\n\nI thought Apple will be very nitpicky with Versions...\nWill a Godot 3.6 export work with modern Xcode and be accepted by Apple Store?\n\nI tried to export to macos on a Monterey emulation and Xcode 14.2, \nbut for Godot 4.5 Stable you need Ventura minimum (AVX2), and a newer Xcode (forgot number)..\n\nSo what's the actual baseline for Apple Store?\nWhat's the min version of Godot that can be used?\n\nAnd the min version of macos or xcode?\nAnd what about the iPhone!\n\nI'm not a macOS user, but I'm considering porting my app to iPhone..\nso much questions so little time! ;)\n \n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328148359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3328806750","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110852#issuecomment-3328806750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110852","id":3328806750,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GaY9e","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T14:24:04Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T14:24:04Z","body":"Updates are already done for 3.x. These changes would be available in upcommin